# Playwright E2E Rule

- Use Playwright + TypeScript.
- Test business journeys, not every visual detail.
- Prefer role/label/text/test-id selectors over brittle CSS/XPath selectors.
- Use `data-testid` only where semantic selectors are insufficient.
- Keep tests independent.
- Never depend on production accounts/data.
- Put reusable authenticated setup in fixtures when authentication is implemented.
- Keep test data creation deterministic.
- Capture traces/screenshots on failure.
- Critical flows eventually include:
  - registration/login,
  - content publishing → user viewing,
  - quiz creation → attempt → result,
  - weekly question → grading,
  - competition score/ranking.
- During skeleton phase, smoke tests may cover navigation only and must be labeled as shell tests.
